CRITICAL MERMAID RULES. The diagram MUST start with `erDiagram`. No other diagram type is allowed.
1. In the DIAGRAM ONLY, use simplified one-word types: INT, BIGINT, SMALLINT, VARCHAR, TEXT,
   DECIMAL, FLOAT, BOOLEAN, DATE, TIMESTAMP, TIMESTAMPTZ, UUID, JSON.
   NO parentheses, commas or spaces in a type: write VARCHAR (not VARCHAR(255)),
   DECIMAL (not DECIMAL(10,2)), BIGINT (not BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY).
   Exact DBMS types belong in the tables of this document, never in the diagram.
2. Attribute line format is exactly: <type> <name> [PK|FK|UK[, PK|FK|UK]]
   name = letters, digits, underscore only. Nothing else on the line:
   no NOT NULL, DEFAULT, UNIQUE, CHECK, REFERENCES, comments.
   Multiple constraints are comma-separated, e.g. `BIGINT order_id PK, FK`.
3. Relationship format: ENTITY_A ||--o{ ENTITY_B : "label"
   The label is mandatory and always in double quotes, with no double quotes inside it.
   Cardinality tokens: left side `||` `|o` `}|` `}o`, right side `||` `o|` `|{` `o{`.
4. Entity names start with a letter and contain only letters, digits and underscores
   (snake_case is fine). No spaces, hyphens or dots. Use the same names in the
   conceptual and logical diagrams.
5. Every entity used in a relationship must also have its own `{ ... }` block.
6. In the LOGICAL diagram, M:N relationships must be drawn through a junction entity.

Example of a valid diagram:
```mermaid
erDiagram
    customers ||--o{ orders : "places"
    orders ||--|{ order_items : "contains"
    products ||--o{ order_items : "appears in"
    customers {
        BIGINT customer_id PK
        VARCHAR email UK
        TIMESTAMPTZ created_at
    }
    orders {
        BIGINT order_id PK
        BIGINT customer_id FK
        DECIMAL total_amount
    }
    order_items {
        BIGINT order_id PK, FK
        BIGINT product_id PK, FK
        INT quantity
    }
    products {
        BIGINT product_id PK
        VARCHAR name
    }
```